    "The Brass Plates",
    "(Under every mask, a small engraved plate.)\n\nDR. A. HALE — 1962\nMRS. HALE — 1962\nMISS ADA CRANE — 1962\nMR. LOWELL — 1962\n(...twenty-six more, all 1962...)\n\nJ. OKAFOR — two years ago\nM. REYES — two years ago\nT. & S. WHITLOCK — last year\nD. ARCENEAUX — last spring\nP. NOVAK — last autumn\n\nR. CALLOWAY — nineteen days ago\n(This mask is not dusty. It is not porcelain either. It is warm.)\n\n(And one empty hook. The plate beneath it is already engraved. The brass is still bright where the tool went in:)\n%s",
